<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49579" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tȳphon</span></b> , ōnis,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυφών</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A violent whirlwind</i>, <i>a
			typhoon</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 2, 48, 49, § 131</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">App de Mundo, p. 64, 5.—The same
					accompanied by lightning,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 3, 130</span></i>
			. Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tȳphōnĭcus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ventus,</span>”
				<i>a typhoon</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Act. 27, 14</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A name given by the king of Egypt to a comet</i> or
				<i>meteor</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 2, 25,
				24, § 91</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
